Local bcachefs packaging
========================

This branch is Debian's debian/experimental packaging with the native
bcachefs storage driver applied on top. It is not intended for upload to
Debian.

Versioning
----------

Local builds carry a +bcachefsN suffix on the Debian revision, for example:

    incus (7.6.0-1~exp1+bcachefs1) experimental; urgency=medium

The suffix is deliberate:

  * "+" sorts after the base version, so the local build replaces the
    matching Debian package.
  * It still sorts before the next Debian upload (~exp2, -1, -2, ...), so
    official packages supersede it again.
  * No epoch is used. An epoch would outrank every future Debian version
    and could not be dropped without a manual downgrade.

Increment the suffix (bcachefs1 -> bcachefs2 -> ...) whenever the packaged
source changes, so that apt offers the new build.

Merging upstream packaging
--------------------------

    git fetch origin
    git merge origin/debian/experimental

Conflicts are normally limited to debian/changelog and the API extension
lists. Resolve the changelog by keeping the local +bcachefs entry on top
with an incremented suffix. Enable `git rerere` to reuse the resolution.

CI
--

.github/workflows/debian-build.yml builds binary packages on
debian:testing and debian:sid and uploads the .deb files as artifacts.
A few build dependencies are only available in Debian experimental; the
workflow adds experimental with a priority-500 pin so the packages still
build against the base suite.
